  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular Poultry in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and Senegal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Senegal and C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire face challenges in their growing poultry sectors such as increased dependency on imports for feed, resource depletion as conventional poultry farming relies heavily on finite resources, and environmental impacts of unprocessed slaughter waste and manure, amongst others. Tackling these in a sustainable way into a circular system offers necessary positive environmental impact, economic benefits and potential for additional jobs.  This study serves to create a circular vision for C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire&#x2019;s and Senegal&#x2019;s poultry sectors and to show the potential for private sector development as well as new Dutch business opportunities in both countries. Circular poultry should support C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire and Senegal in their endeavors to become more self-sufficient in terms of (animal) proteins and thus contribute to (regional) food sovereignty, by proposing and offering circular solutions that allow the countries to leapfrog towards a more resilient food system.</narrative>
  </description>
